# NutriOCR

NutriOCR is a capstone project that explores OCR-based calorie tracking from food packaging labels.
Made by Olga Dobler, OPIT BCs in Computer Science student.

## Technologies

- Python
- PaddleOCR 3.3.3 (PPStructureV3)
- PaddlePaddle 3.2.0 (CPU config)
- OpenAI Vision API (gpt-5)
- Ollama (Gemma3/Gemma4 Vision)

# Hardware

- CPU: Intel(R) Core(TM) i3-14100F
- GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5060 Ti
- Memory: 558 gb
- Internet: Ethernet

## Project Status

Working text recognition pipeline

Current functionality:
- Process food label images
- Extract text using PaddleOCR (on CPU) / Gemma12b & Gemma72b (on GPU) / gpt-5 (via openAI API)
Source files: ocr_paddle.py orc_gemma.py ocr_gpt5.py
- Save the results into json files
- For PaddleOCR: converts .md output into json 
Source file: jsonifier.py
- verificator.py verifies transcripted results upon objective values
- model_scores.md keeps the results: accuracy, expenses

